ce</strong>.</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:163px\">\n\t\t\t<div>25%</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:143px\">\n\t\t\t<div>Final presentation</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:331px\">\n\t\t\t<div>Each group&rsquo;s presentation should be about 20-25&nbsp;minutes. <strong>The slides should be uploaded to iLearn and <u>sent to the comment group</u> 5 days in advance</strong>.</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:163px\">\n\t\t\t<div>30%</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:1px solid black; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:143px\">\n\t\t\t<div>Class participation (including attendance)</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; vertical-align:top; width:331px\">\n\t\t\t<div>Attendance and performance in the class discussions and activities.</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t\t<td style=\"border-bottom:1px solid black; border-left:none; border-right:1px solid black; border-top:none; width:163px\">\n\t\t\t<div>30%</div>\n\t\t\t</td>\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n",
    "course_pol": null,
    "course_pol_en": "1. The class will be suspended once on 11/17 due to the instructor’s participation in an international conference, and make-up classes will be arranged.\n\n2. Please make sure to attend the first class, as it will cover the course structure, grading criteria, and group assignments.\n\n3. Please register on MyFCU if you need to take leave. You must provide the reason for the leave and attach supporting documents. Do not miss classes more than 3 times.\n\n4. We have some cases for class discussion. Please read these cases before class. During class, we will use group discussions or random assignments to have students answer questions. You are encouraged to participate in group discussions and share your thoughts in class.\n\n5. You are encouraged to actively participate in class activities. After each class, group leaders must record how many times each member answered questions and hand it to the instructor. Active participation will improve your class participation grade. However, this count does not include group discussion presentations.\n\n6. You must submit a peer evaluation form, rating each group member (excluding yourself) on a scale from 1 to 10. You are also encouraged to describe each member's contributions in detail.\n\n7. You can download the pre-class slides for each chapter from iLearn to use in class. Additionally, the after-class slides will be uploaded after the completion of each chapter.",
    "course_rem": null,
    "course_rem_en": null,
    "ais_meno": null,
    "ais_meno_en": "<div>Learning must be based on honesty. Any student who attempts to use a work that he has not produced as his own is considered dishonest. Students who cheat or plagiarize in homework, tests or exams, or assist others, will be scored as zero. If they are repeat offenders, they will be submitted in accordance with the rewards and punishments for students of Feng Chia University.</div>\n\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n\n<div>1. Students should have a strong understanding of copyright and avoid using pirated books.</div>\n\n<div>2. Students must uphold good academic ethics, which includes not only avoiding plagiarism but also properly citing sources for all referenced materials.</div>\n\n<div>3. Students should interact positively with their peers in class to foster strong interpersonal relationships.</div>\n",
    "ilearn_mk": "N"
  },
